% --- Graduation Thesis ---
\noindent
\textbf{\color{primary}Graduation Thesis: CV Health Intelligence System} \hfill \textcolor{darkgray}{\small Mar 2026 -- Jul 2026}\\[1pt]
\hfill \href{https://cv-assistant.vercel.app}{\textcolor{secondary}{\small \faGlobe\ Live Demo}} \quad \href{https://github.com/dungken/cv-assistant}{\textcolor{secondary}{\small \faGithub\ Source Code}}\\[2pt]
{\small\textbf{Stack:} \textbf{C\# / ASP.NET Core} (API Gateway), Python / FastAPI (AI services), React + TypeScript (FE), PostgreSQL, ChromaDB, Docker}\\[2pt]
{\small\textit{A microservices-based platform that tracks the ``freshness'' of a candidate's CV against real-time job market data, identifies skill gaps, and recommends an optimized learning path to maximize job opportunities.}}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=14pt,itemsep=2pt,topsep=3pt,label={•}]
    \item \textbf{.NET API Gateway:} Built the central \textbf{ASP.NET Core} API Gateway handling request routing, \textbf{JWT authentication}, rate limiting, and response aggregation from downstream Python/FastAPI microservices.
    \item \textbf{Microservices Architecture:} Designed the system with clear service boundaries -- \textbf{.NET} owns the API and auth layer; \textbf{Python/FastAPI} owns AI services (CV Freshness Scoring, Learning Path Optimizer, NLP skill extraction via mBERT); \textbf{React + TypeScript} renders the dashboard.
    \item \textbf{Database Design:} Modeled a time-series schema in \textbf{PostgreSQL} for daily skill demand tracking (~200 JD/day crawled from ITviec/TopCV). Integrated \textbf{ChromaDB} for semantic vector search on job descriptions.
    \item \textbf{Core Research:} Proposed and validated the \textbf{CV Freshness Score} formula (trend weight, recency, skill importance). Benchmarked 3 Learning Path optimization algorithms (Greedy, Dijkstra, Dynamic Programming) on a skill graph of 500+ nodes and 50 test cases.
\end{itemize}

